    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d233">

                <pb facs="0507" n="423" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg423"/>

                <head>No. 229.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir L.
                            West to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-11-01"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 1, 1886</date>.
                        [Received November. 2.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note of the 9th of
                    August last, respecting the treatment of the United “States fishing boat Rattler
                    by the <pb facs="0508" n="424" xml:id="pg424"/> Canadian authorities, I have the
                    honor to inclose to you herewith, in obedience to the instructions of the Earl
                    of Iddesleigh, copy of a dispatch from the administrator of the Government of
                    Canada together with copy of the report of the collector of customs at
                    Shelburne.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>L. S. SACKVILLE WEST.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d233-a1.xml" xpointer="d233-a1"/>
